Spec: specs/000-foundation/spec.md (AC6-AC12); ADR 0002; research Q7
Why this approach: every error line is built from config.Error fields or a fixed reason, never err.Error(): flag, yaml, net and syscall messages can all quote the value. -h exits 0 before config loads, so help works even with a broken config.yaml.
Trade-off / known limit: AC6's shutdown_timeout value is observed without a test route (T8): a half-sent request keeps the connection active, so Shutdown gives up after env's 100ms instead of the file's 1h, and run exits 1. Positional arguments are still ignored.
Verified by: GOFLAGS=-count=1 make verify; go test -race -count=5 ./cmd/gateway. TestRun_Help (-h, -help, --help with an invalid config.yaml and env), TestRun_InvalidFlags, TestRun_EnvOverridesFile, TestRun_LogLevel, TestRun_UnknownKey, TestRun_InvalidEnvLogLevel, TestRun_InvalidEnvShutdownTimeout, TestRun_EmptyEnvIsUnset, TestRun_EmptyConfigFile, TestRun_InvalidAddressFailsBeforeBind, TestRun_BindErrors; the AC8-AC10 tests find no sentinel (or abc) in the output.
